{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":1129,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Hos.8","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Hosea","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Hosea 8","reference":"Hosea 8","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"Almost every verse of this chapter speaks both the sins and punishment of Israel, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-14.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":4,"text":"Set the trumpet - The Lord here commands the prophet to publish, as by sound of trumpet, that which God will bring upon apostate Israel.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":5,"text":"He - The king of Assyria.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":6,"text":"As an eagle - Swift, hungry, surmounting all difficulties.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":7,"text":"House of the Lord - The family of Israel, the Israelites church.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":9,"text":"Shall cry - But not sincerely.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":10,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":11,"text":"They - Israel.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":12,"text":"Kings - Shallum, Menahem, Pekah, and Hosea.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":13,"text":"Not by me - Not by my direction.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":14,"text":"Knew it not - Did not approve of it.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":15,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":16,"text":"Thy calf - The chief idol set up in Samaria.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":17,"text":"Cast thee off - Hath provoked God to cast thee off.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":18,"text":"Against them - Idols, and idol worshippers.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":19,"text":"How long - How long will it be, ere they repent and reform?","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":20,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":21,"text":"From Israel - By their invention.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":22,"text":"It - Both the idol and the worshippers of it.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":23,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":24,"text":"Sown the wind - A proverbial speech to denote lost labour.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":25,"text":"Whirlwind - A tempest, which destroyeth all that is in its way; an emblem of the wrath of God.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":26,"text":"No stalk - All your dependance on idols, and foreign assistance, will be as seed that bear neither stalk nor bud.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":27,"text":"No meal - Or suppose it produced stalk and bud, yet the bud shall be blasted, and never yield meal.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":28,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":29,"text":"Gone up - Israel is like a wild ass.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":30,"text":"A wild ass - Stubborn, wild, untamed.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":31,"text":"Alone - Solitary, where is no path or tract; so they were in their captivity.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":32,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":33,"text":"Gather them - I will assemble them together, that they may be taken and destroyed together.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":34,"text":"A little - For a while before their final captivity.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":35,"text":"The burden - The tribute laid on them by the king.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":36,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":37,"text":"Altars - Those which they shall find in Assyria.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":38,"text":"To sin - Shall be the occasion of his greater guilt and punishment.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":39,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":40,"text":"Written - By Moses first, by other prophets afterwards.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":41,"text":"But they were counted - Israel looks on them, as nothing to them.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":42,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":43,"text":"They shall return - Many shall fly from the Assyrian into Egypt.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":44,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":45,"text":"Temples - Idol temples.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":46,"text":"Devour the palaces - This was fulfilled when all the cities of Judah and Israel were laid in ashes by the king of Assyria.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Hosea","chapter":8}}